 "note": "Three changes, each measured separately. (1) The pair kernel took one invocation per atom and looped over the 27 cells of the neighbour shell; it now takes one invocation per (atom, cell), which is the same work with 27x the threads. (2) minimum_image64 subtracted one box at a time under a loop bounded at 64; it is now loop-free. (3) A `cell/wrap` pass folds every coordinate into [0, box) once per step, so the pair kernel's minimum image is one conditional shift. All three are exact: the fixed-point accumulators are order-independent, and the wrap returns the same image bit for bit, which the cell-list check confirms at a worst force difference of 0.",
